{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe day was full. I visited the Esterhazy gallery again this morning, from nine until eleven. The Prince, hearing a professor from Berlin was in his city, had a valet show me everything, including the private cabinet. It is impressive, though one sees the taste of a collector rather than the spirit of a state.\n\nI lunched at an inn with Professor Sonnleitner, director of the antiquities cabinet, and a gentleman from Padua. We spoke of antiquities, but mostly of the state of German scholarship. The wine was good, and the company polite, if a bit dull.\n\nIn the evening, I went to the opera to hear Rossini’s *Corradino*. The music is a storm of sensation, loud and fast, lacking the deep, quiet structure of the old German masters. It appeals to the ear but leaves the mind unengaged. I am tired now, and the heat in the room is oppressive. I miss the cool of our study in Berlin. Give my love to the boys.\n\nYour affectionate,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080357,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":231,"prompt_tokens":951,"total_tokens":1182,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-s9kH3dcrrPOzxNSkABBEAYhVsInGR0cz","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":951,"prompt_ms":935.067,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9832460567823343,"prompt_per_second":1017.0394207046126,"predicted_n":231,"predicted_ms":5552.725,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.142282608695655,"predicted_per_second":41.42110405251475}}